# Plain .trivyignore — this is trivy's own DEFAULT ignorefile (repo root,
# `--ignorefile` default), auto-loaded by every gate that doesn't override it.
# In this repo that's the org-shared `scan / Vulnerability Scan (Trivy)` gate
# (.github/workflows/security.yml → ADORSYS-GIS/ai-governance
# security-gates.yml, pinned SHA, `scanners: vuln,secret,misconfig`) — it
# passes NO `trivyignores`/`ignorefile` input to aquasecurity/trivy-action, so
# trivy falls back to this file. It's DIFFERENT from .trivyignore.yaml (whose
# `paths:` scheme is `rendered/<chart>.yaml`, a single flat file per chart —
# matches ONLY release-helm-charts.yml's deterministic scan, which renders
# each chart to `rendered/<chart>.yaml` before scanning; it structurally
# cannot match paths this gate reports, which are directory-relative,
# e.g. `librechat-code-interpreter/templates/worker-sandbox-deployment.yaml`,
# since this gate scans `charts/` directly with trivy's own Helm renderer).
#
# ⚠️ This trivy version's plain .trivyignore is ID-ONLY for misconfigurations
# — no path-scoping (tested: a trailing path token on the line is silently
# ignored, verified empirically against a wrong path). Every entry below is
# therefore a genuine BLANKET ignore of the rule ID, not scoped to one file,
# unlike .trivyignore.yaml's policy of "never a blanket whole-ID ignore" — the
# tool doesn't give this gate that option. Verified (2026-08-07) that no OTHER
# dependency-free chart in this repo trips these three IDs today (the gate
# only manages to render dependency-free charts — every chart with a subchart
# dependency fails to render under a bare checkout with no `helm dependency
# build` and is silently skipped, so it never reaches this ignorefile at all).
# If a FUTURE chart legitimately needs one of these IDs to fail, this file
# will incorrectly hide it — revisit this note before adding another
# workload that needs elevated capabilities or a non-default securityContext.

# KSV-0005 / KSV-0014 / KSV-0118 — charts/librechat-code-interpreter's
# sandbox-runner container ONLY (ADR-0122). NsJail's namespace/mount/chroot
# setup genuinely requires SYS_ADMIN + friends (see
# charts/librechat-code-interpreter/templates/worker-sandbox-deployment.yaml
# for the full capability list and the KVM-mode alternative that wouldn't
# need any of this), which forces a non-default securityContext (KSV-0118)
# and rules out readOnlyRootFilesystem (KSV-0014 — NsJail writes its per-job
# workspace/scratch dirs to the container rootfs). Every OTHER container in
# this chart (api, file-server, tool-call-server, egress-gateway,
# service-worker, both busybox init containers) IS hardened, not ignored —
# see the same templates dir for the codeapi.hardened*SecurityContext helpers
# applied everywhere except sandbox-runner.
KSV-0005
KSV-0014
KSV-0118
